{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The multimeter and heat shrink tubing fit my breadboards, battery holders, circuit boards, and relay: they help me test circuits and insulate wire connections.",
    "The smaller caliper fits measuring components for project assembly. Removable fastening also fits my past purchases, though I would wait for a specific mounting job before choosing the VELCRO."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The larger caliper offers measuring capacity I do not currently need, and the nut assortment is hard to choose without knowing whether its thread sizes fit my project.",
    "The adhesive, fluorescent tape, and cutting wheels require specific jobs I have not indicated. My caster purchase also does not mean I need a separate hand truck."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in practical project supplies seems to have been stretched into a broad interest in workshop products, even when their purpose differs from assembling small circuits.",
    "Past fastening and caster purchases seem to have been treated as ongoing needs for more securing and moving equipment."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my electrical components matters: testing voltages and insulating wiring are concrete next steps that make those parts usable together.",
    "I choose tools and supplies when their size, compatibility, and purpose fit a particular task; a broadly useful item alone is not enough for me to buy it now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my small electronics projects but stretched that interest too broadly into general workshop and moving supplies."
}"}
